experiment: framehold
  instrument        framehold   trial seed 000000000135d3c8   1200000 ticks
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  seed family       offset 512821 -> first creature 00000000013cfafe  (nonzero = the
                    REPLICATION; family 0 gave one arm of four at +3.5 SE)
  what happened     `framecopy` looked spectacular and was trivial: the voice
                    alternated at the caregiver's rate because a SHIPPED
                    inhibitory auditory->vocal tract stops the babbling while
                    the creature hears something. An interrupt, not a frame.
  the tell          `heard` duty sat BELOW the silent baseline -- gated OFF --
                    while `oracle` rose to 0.83, driven ON. Anti-phase reflex,
                    not an oscillator.
  the discriminator PERSISTENCE, which is what made M1b real rather than a
                    pass-through: a reflex dies with its driver, an internal
                    beat rings on. Pulse 4 s, then SILENCE 4 s, and measure the
                    f-component DURING THE SILENCE.
  v1 WAS CONFOUNDED and this is the fix. Fixed 4 s holds repeat at 0.25 Hz,
    and every f tested is an exact harmonic of that -- so the single offset
    transient deposited power at precisely the measured frequency, with no
    rhythm required, right where v1's effect sat. The phase-tiling I was
    careful about is what CAUSED it.
  the correction    hold lengths now VARY (3.0/4.5/3.5/5.0/4.0 s) so transients
                    land incoherently, and the phase reference is ABSOLUTE
                    TIME so a ring-out inheriting the drive's phase still sums.
  not fakeable by   a slowly decaying inhibition returns the voice SMOOTHLY to
  a slow leak       baseline, which is broadband. Only continued ALTERNATION
                    puts power at f.

  PRE-REGISTERED
    positive control  `heard` SNR during the DRIVE must be large. If it is not,
                      the reflex is not even engaging and nothing else reads.
    persistence       `heard` hold-SNR >= 2.0 AND >= 3 SE over the matching
                      `silent` arm -> the beat outlasts its driver, which is a
                      FRAME rather than an interrupt.
    reflex only       hold-SNR at the silent baseline -> it dies with the
                      driver. No frame, and an internal oscillator on the
                      voicing gate becomes the next build.
    decay             early vs late halves of the hold, reported either way.
                      A real ring-out decays; a constant offset would suggest
                      the statistic is picking up something structural.

